{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-fix-expr-sql/agg-result-type-decimal",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-SQL-1",
    "SQL-AGG-TYPE"
  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-sql-1/agg-result-type: ND was never created (3292). Asks, over the stored Decimal x of ND (made by ADO DDL, SQL literals), what result Field.Type, Size, Precision, Scale and value type Sum, Avg, Min and Max give, each in its own statement over the rows without the 99999999999999.9999 row, then Sum over all rows. The stored rows are read back first. Fixture r-fix-expr-sql-sql1 is opened read-only through DAO.DBEngine.120; each recordset reads Name, Type and Value of every field. Each statement is preceded by a marker (a DROP TABLE of a table that does not exist, which always fails), so DBEngine.Errors read after the statement shows that statement's own failure or the marker's, never an older one. Where Field Precision and Scale are read, the recordset is first positioned on its first row (MoveFirst) and DecimalPlaces is not read.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
